{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.3648239564002363, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["Gain is within noise: 0.3648 vs incumbent 0.3653 is a 0.0005 improvement against per-job noise sd ~0.0037; recomputed z ~ 0.11. Provisional reject is consistent with the numbers, and only one candidate run exists.", "Minor robustness risk: MurckoScaffold.MurckoScaffoldSmiles can raise on unparseable SMILES and returns '' for acyclic molecules, so all acyclic molecules collapse into one large bucket and get systematically down-weighted. A try/except with a per-molecule fallback key would be safer.", "Scaffold-frequency weighting is aligned with the harness's scaffold-grouped folds, so part of any gain may be specific to the CV protocol rather than generalization. It is computed only from train_smiles, so this is legitimate modelling, not measurement circumvention.", "Added complexity (Counter, MurckoScaffold import, weight plumbing into two models) buys no measurable gain, against the simpler-is-better guidance."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Weight each training molecule by 1/sqrt(size of its Murcko scaffold family), normalized to mean 1, and pass these as sample_weight to both the LightGBM and SVR fits so large scaffold families do not dominate training.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b016", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.36527898176320217, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.36527898176320217, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B2_caco_SS_2_s1-candidate-7_1795059368091", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00196994, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00196994, "latency_s": 8.421078708022833, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 6803, "tokens_out": 1745}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.1201506, "cost_usd_plan": 0.1201506, "latency_s": 25.408908509009052, "requested_model": "opus", "role": "critic", "served_model